    <exercise workspace="1in">
        <p>
            Consider the visual pattern shown below. Describe the pattern and draw the next step.  
        </p>
        <image source="VP_rev3.png" width="75%">
            <shortdescription>A visual pattern showing stacked squares of 1, 5, 11, 19. </shortdescription>
        </image>
        <solution>
            <p>
                At each step of the pattern a number of additional squares, equal to the step number are added to both
                the left and right side of the pattern.  To create the fifth step of the pattern we would take the pattern
                from step 4 and add 5 square to the left and 5 squares to the right.  
            </p>
            <image source="VP_rev3A.png" width="40%">
                <shortdescription>A pattern with 29 squares.</shortdescription>
            </image>
        </solution>
    </exercise>

     <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Consider the following table which lists the odd numbers from 1 to 97.
            </p>
            <tabular halign="center" top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
                <row>
                    <cell>1</cell>
                    <cell>3</cell>
                    <cell>5</cell>
                    <cell>7</cell>
                    <cell>9</cell>
                    <cell>11</cell>
